rs.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>conductor<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>conductor<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>conduct<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: orchestra conductor \/ electrical conductor \/ bus conductor \/ train conductor<\/span><\/p><p>similar: director \/ maestro \/ guide \/ usher<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: insulator \/ nonconductor \/ obstructor<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"conductor","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"new","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-16T17:06:54+00:00"},{"id":51312,"front":"<p>Starting a new business is a risky _______, but it can be very rewarding. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ \u00fczleti kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>The government launched a new _______ to tackle unemployment in rural areas. <em>(projekt \/ kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s)<\/em><\/p><p>Her latest novel is an ambitious literary _______, blending historical fact with fantasy. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ irodalmi k\u00eds\u00e9rlet)<\/em><\/p><p>The spirit of free _______ is crucial for economic growth and innovation. <em>(v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ gazdas\u00e1gi tev\u00e9kenys\u00e9g)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s \/ kezdem\u00e9nyez\u00e9s \/ v\u00e1llalat<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): passzivit\u00e1s \/ tehetetlens\u00e9g \/ kudarcos pr\u00f3b\u00e1lkoz\u00e1s<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 free _______ = szabad v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. The principles of free _______ are fundamental to capitalism.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 private _______ = mag\u00e1nv\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. The country encourages private _______ and foreign investment.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a joint _______ = k\u00f6z\u00f6s v\u00e1llalkoz\u00e1s (pl. They formed a joint _______ to develop the new software.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 spirit of _______ = v\u00e1llalkoz\u00f3 szellem (pl. The city has a strong spirit of _______ and innovation.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>enterprise<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>enterprising<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>enterprise<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: business enterprise \/ commercial enterprise \/ public enterprise \/ new enterprise<\/span><\/p><p>similar: venture \/ undertaking \/ project \/ company<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: inactivity \/ stagnation \/ passivity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"enterprise","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"1.5 \u00f3ra","good":"2 \u00f3ra","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-16T19:07:24+00:00"},{"id":51302,"front":"<p>She felt herself grow dizzy and __________, so she sat down quickly. <em>(el\u00e1jul \/ rosszul lesz)<\/em><\/p><p>The old photograph had a __________ sepia tone, making the faces barely visible. <em>(halv\u00e1ny \/ fak\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p>Despite the strong evidence, the defendant offered only a __________ denial. <em>(gyenge \/ er\u0151tlen)<\/em><\/p><p>A __________ hope flickered in his heart that he might still find his way home. <em>(halv\u00e1ny \/ gyenge)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">el\u00e1jul \/ halv\u00e1ny \/ gyenge<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): er\u0151s \/ \u00e9l\u00e9nk \/ \u00f6ntudatos<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 feel _________ = rosszul \u00e9rzi mag\u00e1t, el\u00e1jul (pl. He felt faint after donating blood.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _________ light = halv\u00e1ny f\u00e9ny (pl. Only a faint light filtered through the curtains.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _________ hope = halv\u00e1ny rem\u00e9ny (pl. There was a faint hope that they would be rescued.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _________ smell = gyenge szag (pl. I detected a faint smell of smoke.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a _________ memory = halv\u00e1ny eml\u00e9k (pl. She had only a faint memory of her childhood home.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>faint<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>faint<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>faintly<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>faint<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>faint<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: faint light \/ faint hope \/ faint smell \/ faint memory<\/span><\/p><p>similar: dizzy \/ weak \/ pale \/ indistinct<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: strong \/ bright \/ clear<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"45 perc","good":"1 \u00f3ra","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-13T12:18:37+00:00"},{"id":51311,"front":"<p>The manager decided to _______ the employee for repeated lateness. <em>(elbocs\u00e1t \/ kir\u00fag)<\/em><\/p><p>Let&#039;s _______ these minor concerns for now and focus on the main issue. <em>(elvet \/ mell\u0151z)<\/em><\/p><p>The judge will _______ the case if there isn&#039;t enough evidence. <em>(elutas\u00edt \/ ejt)<\/em><\/p><p>She tried to _______ his fears with a comforting smile, but he remained anxious. <em>(elhesseget \/ el\u0171z)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">elbocs\u00e1t \/ elvet \/ elutas\u00edt<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): felvesz \/ elfogad \/ megfontol<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a case = \u00fcgyet elutas\u00edt\/ejt (pl. The court decided to _______ the case due to lack of evidence.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an idea\/suggestion = \u00f6tletet\/javaslatot elvet (pl. They chose to _______ the idea of expanding abroad for now.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an employee = alkalmazottat elbocs\u00e1t (pl. The company had to _______ several employees during the recession.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a complaint = panaszt elutas\u00edt (pl. The customer service department decided to _______ her complaint.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a thought\/fear = gondolatot\/f\u00e9lelmet elhesseget (pl. He tried to _______ the negative thoughts from his mind.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>dismiss<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>dismissive<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>dismissively<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>dismissal<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>dismiss<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: dismiss a claim \/ dismiss an appeal \/ dismiss an argument \/ dismiss out of hand<\/span><\/p><p>similar: reject \/ disregard \/ fire \/ release<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: accept \/ consider \/ employ<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"dismiss\ndismissive\ndismissively","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-16T18:39:27+00:00"},{"id":51323,"front":"<p>After years of touring, the popular rock band decided to _______ and pursue solo careers. <em>(feloszlatja mag\u00e1t \/ sz\u00e9toszlik)<\/em><\/p><p>The government announced its intention to _______ the special task force once its mission was complete. <em>(feloszlat \/ megsz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>Due to lack of funding, the research group had no choice but to _______ its operations. <em>(felsz\u00e1mol \/ besz\u00fcntet)<\/em><\/p><p>The general ordered his troops to _______ and return to their respective garrisons. <em>(sz\u00e9tsz\u00e9led \/ feloszlik)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">feloszlat \/ sz\u00e9toszlat \/ felsz\u00e1mol<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00f6sszegy\u0171jt \/ alak\u00edt \/ szervez<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a band = feloszlatni egy zenekart (pl. They decided to _______ a band after their last album.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ an army = feloszlatni egy hadsereget (pl. The treaty required them to _______ an army.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a committee = feloszlatni egy bizotts\u00e1got (pl. The chairman chose to _______ a committee.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 to _______ a group = feloszlatni egy csoportot (pl. The leader had to _______ a group due to internal conflicts.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>disbandment<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>disband<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: disband a group \/ disband an organization \/ disband a committee \/ disband a military unit<\/span><\/p><p>similar: dissolve \/ break up \/ demobilize \/ scatter<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: assemble \/ form \/ create<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"disband","study_direction":"back_to_front","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"new","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-16T17:08:08+00:00"},{"id":51309,"front":"<p>I&#039;ve never seen _______ a beautiful sunset before! <em>(olyan \/ ilyen)<\/em><\/p><p>He is _______ a talented musician that he often plays multiple instruments. <em>(annyira \/ olyan m\u00e9rt\u00e9kben)<\/em><\/p><p>The report highlighted _______ issues as climate change and resource depletion. <em>(olyan \/ p\u00e9ld\u00e1ul)<\/em><\/p><p>It was _______ a relief to finally finish the project after months of hard work. <em>(ekkora \/ ilyen nagy)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">olyan \/ ilyen \/ annyira<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): semmilyen \/ egy\u00e1ltal\u00e1n nem \/ m\u00e1smilyen<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ as = olyan, mint \/ p\u00e9ld\u00e1ul (pl. Problems _______ as pollution and poverty need urgent attention.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a lot = nagyon sok (pl. He eats _______ a lot of chocolate.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ a shame = micsoda sz\u00e9gyen \/ milyen k\u00e1r (pl. It&#039;s _______ a shame you can&#039;t come to the party.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ is life = ilyen az \u00e9let<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>such<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: such a \/ such as \/ such an \/ such that<\/span><\/p><p>similar: like this \/ of this kind \/ so \/ this kind of<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: different \/ dissimilar \/ unlike<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"1.5 \u00f3ra","good":"2 \u00f3ra","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-16T19:05:44+00:00"},{"id":51320,"front":"<p>After years of practice, she became incredibly _______ in playing the piano, effortlessly performing complex pieces. <em>(\u00fcgyes \/ j\u00e1rtas)<\/em><\/p><p>To be truly _______ in a foreign language, one must not only understand grammar but also grasp cultural nuances. <em>(foly\u00e9kony \/ magabiztos)<\/em><\/p><p>The new software engineer is highly _______ in Python and C++, making him a valuable asset to the development team. <em>(szak\u00e9rt\u0151 \/ kompetens)<\/em><\/p><p>Her _______ command of legal terminology impressed the judges during the trial. <em>(mesteri \/ kiv\u00e1l\u00f3)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #22c55e\">j\u00e1rtas \/ \u00fcgyes \/ szak\u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p><span style=\"background-color: #f3f4f6; padding: 2px 6px; border-radius: 4px\">Negative meaning (HU): \u00fcgyetlen \/ tudatlan \/ hozz\u00e1 nem \u00e9rt\u0151<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ in something = j\u00e1rtas valamiben (pl. He is proficient in several programming languages.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 highly _______ = nagyon j\u00e1rtas (pl. She is highly proficient at public speaking.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 become _______ = j\u00e1rtass\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. With practice, you will become proficient.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ user = j\u00e1rtas felhaszn\u00e1l\u00f3 (pl. The software is designed for proficient users.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>proficient<\/strong><\/p><p>adverb: <strong>proficiently<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>proficiency<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: proficient in \/ highly proficient \/ become proficient \/ proficient user<\/span><\/p><p>similar: skilled \/ competent \/ expert \/ adept<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: unskilled \/ incompetent \/ inexperienced<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":"proficient\nproficiently\nproficiency","study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"new","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"2 perc","good":"10 perc","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":null},{"id":51297,"front":"<p>After hours of cooking, the vegetables turned into a soft, unappetizing _______. <em>(p\u00e9pes massza \/ k\u00e1sa)<\/em><\/p><p>His sentimental speech was full of emotional _______, rather than concrete arguments. <em>(\u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g \/ ny\u00e1ladz\u00e1s)<\/em><\/p><p>The prolonged rain turned the hiking trail into a muddy _______, making progress difficult. <em>(s\u00e1r \/ dagony\u00e1s talaj)<\/em><\/p><p>Don't _______ the potatoes too much; we want them creamy, not a watery paste. <em>(p\u00e9pes\u00edt \/ sz\u00e9tnyom)<\/em><\/p><p><span style=\"color: rgb(34, 197, 94);\">p\u00e9pes\u00edt \/ p\u00e9pes massza \/ \u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g \/ p\u00e9pes<\/span><\/p><p><span>Negative meaning (HU): szil\u00e1rd \/ kem\u00e9ny \/ t\u00f6m\u00f6r<\/span><\/p><p>\ud83d\udd11 Tanul\u00e1si megjegyz\u00e9s<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 turn to _______ = p\u00e9pes massz\u00e1v\u00e1 v\u00e1lik (pl. The overcooked apples turned to _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 emotional _______ = \u00e9rzelg\u0151ss\u00e9g (pl. Her letter was full of emotional _______.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 a muddy _______ = s\u00e1ros massza\/dagony\u00e1s talaj (pl. The field was a muddy _______ after the storm.)<\/p><p>\ud83d\udc49 _______ up = p\u00e9pesre nyom (pl. You need to _______ up the bananas for the baby.)<\/p>","front_notes":null,"front_speak":null,"back":"<p><strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p>adjective: <strong>mushy<\/strong><\/p><p>noun: <strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p>verb: <strong>mush<\/strong><\/p><p><span style=\"color: #3b82f6\">common pair: baby mush \/ apple mush \/ emotional mush \/ turn to mush<\/span><\/p><p>similar: pulp \/ paste \/ slop \/ sentimentality<\/p><p><span style=\"color: #ef4444\">negative: solidity \/ firmness \/ clarity<\/span><\/p>","back_notes":null,"back_speak":null,"study_direction":"front_to_back","color":"#6366f1","review":{"state":"learning","interval":0,"lapses":0,"is_leech":false},"previews":{"again":"1 perc","hard":"9 \u00f3ra","good":"1 nap","easy":"2 nap"},"other_side_due_at":"2026-05-18T17:09:48+00:00"}]},"url":"\/flashcards\/10\/study","version":"e2b22e37706595fec52e55935d2eb5d9","sharedProps":["errors","name","auth","sidebarO